</span><span style="--shiki-light:#c62739;--shiki-dark:#F97583">|</span><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF">{" null"}</span></code><div class="twoslash-popup-docs vp-doc"><p>{"The "}<strong><code>getElementById()</code></strong>{" method of the Document interface returns an Element object representing the element whose id property matches the specified string. Since element IDs are required to be unique if specified, they're a useful way to get access to a specific element quickly."}</p></div></span></template></div></span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">(</span><span style="--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;">'foo'</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">).</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;"><div class="v-popper v-popper--theme-twoslash v-popper--theme-dropdown twoslash-hover"><span>className</span><template><span class="twoslash-popup-container vp-copy-ignore"><code class="twoslash-popup-code"><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8">Element.className: string</span></code><div class="twoslash-popup-docs vp-doc"><p>{"The "}<strong><code>className</code></strong>{" property of the Element interface gets and sets the value of the class attribute of the specified element."}</p>{"\n"}<p><a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/docs/Web/API/Element/className">MDN Reference</a></p></div></span></template></div></span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">{" "}</span><span style="--shiki-light:#c62739;--shiki-dark:#F97583;">=</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">{" "}</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;"><div class="v-popper v-popper--theme-twoslash v-popper--theme-dropdown twoslash-hover"><span>classes</span><template><span class="twoslash-popup-container vp-copy-ignore"><code class="twoslash-popup-code"><span style="--shiki-light:#c62739;--shiki-dark:#F97583">const</span><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF">{" classes"}</span><span style="--shiki-light:#c62739;--shiki-dark:#F97583">:</span><span style="--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0">{" CSSModuleClasses"}</span></code></span></template></div></span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">.</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;"><div class="v-popper v-popper--theme-twoslash v-popper--theme-dropdown twoslash-hover"><span>red</span><template><span class="twoslash-popup-container vp-copy-ignore"><code class="twoslash-popup-code"><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8">CSSModuleClasses[string]: string</span></code></span></template></div></span></span></code></pre></div><p>{"CSS modules behavior can be configured via the "}<a href="/config/shared-options#css-modules"><code>css.modules</code>{" option"}</a>.</p><p>{"If "}<code>css.modules.localsConvention</code>{" is set to enable camelCase locals (e.g. "}<code>localsConvention: 'camelCaseOnly'</code>), you can also use named imports:</p><div class="language-js"><button title="Copy code" data-copied="Copied" class="copy"></button><span class="lang">js</span><pre class="shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark twoslash lsp" style="--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e;" tabindex="0" dir="ltr"><code><span class="line"><span style="--shiki-light:#62687b;--shiki-dark:#818e99;">// .apply-color -&gt; applyColor</span></span>{"\n"}<span class="line"><span style="--shiki-light:#c62739;--shiki-dark:#F97583;">import</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">{" { "}</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;"><div class="v-popper v-popper--theme-twoslash v-popper--theme-dropdown twoslash-hover"><span>applyColor</span><template><span class="twoslash-popup-container vp-copy-ignore"><code class="twoslash-popup-code"><span style="--shiki-light:#c62739;--shiki-dark:#F97583">